title: Implement stop-and-drain channel/scope shutdown
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: medium
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-04T05:31:38'
updated_at: '2026-06-13T14:19:43'
result: 'Stop-and-drain shutdown verified and documented as the semantics of `stop`.
  Both actor shapes already drain: message actors use jinn_chan_recv (drains then
  EOS), loop actors use jinn_chan_try_recv (returns buffered msgs even after close,
  -1 only when empty+closed). So `stop` = graceful stop-and-drain, no message loss
  — confirmed by new conformance test loop_actor_stop_drains_all_messages (1..8 all
  processed after stop). Combined with new `join`, graceful shutdown is `stop w` then
  `join w`. Fast/hard termination is deliberately the cancellation path under structured
  `together` scopes (task 2-6), documented in docs/concurrency.md new section "`stop`
  is stop-and-drain; cancellation is the fast path".'
description: 'Implement stop-and-drain shutdown (review 12_safety; builds on task
  2-8''s observable send-after-close). Current state: `close {ch}` exists; receive
  drains buffer after close (pinned by channel_receive_drains_buffer in tests/concurrency_shutdown.rs);
  send-after-close returns false (pinned by send_after_close_is_observable). Missing:
  a scope/actor-level ''stop then drain remaining messages then exit'' primitive so
  an actor can be told to finish queued work before terminating, distinct from hard
  stop. Deliverable: `stop {actor} after drain` (or design-approved surface) lowering
  through src/codegen/mir_codegen/magic.rs + runtime/sched.c support. Definition of
  done: tests in tests/concurrency_shutdown.rs proving no message loss on graceful
  shutdown and bounded termination on hard stop.'
